      "claim": "System dynamics was created in the mid-1950s by Jay W. Forrester at MIT. He published the first results as a 1958 Harvard Business Review article and expanded them into the first book in the field, Industrial Dynamics, in 1961. He developed the approach while studying a General Electric appliance factory, building a simulation which showed that management practices rather than market forces were causing its boom-and-bust cycle.",
