      "claim": "A delay in a balancing loop makes a system likely to oscillate. In physical, exponentially growing systems there must be at least one reinforcing loop driving the growth and at least one balancing loop constraining it, because no system can grow forever in a finite environment.",
      "title": "Donella H. Meadows, Thinking in Systems: A Primer, Chelsea Green Publishing, 2008, on balancing and reinforcing feedback loops",
      "url": "https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/3828902-thinking-in-systems",
