      "claim": "The grouped operation is not an invention of any one library: Wickham named and analysed the split-apply-combine strategy — break a large problem into manageable pieces, operate on each piece independently, then reassemble them — in the Journal of Statistical Software in 2011, describing it as a strategy that applies regardless of how the data is stored.",
