      "claim": "Copy-on-write became the default and only mode in pandas 3.0, released on 21 January 2026. Every object returned from an indexing operation now behaves as an independent copy, memory being shared internally until one side is mutated. The SettingWithCopyWarning was removed because the view or copy ambiguity that produced it no longer exists, and chained assignment now consistently fails, raising a ChainedAssignmentError rather than silently doing nothing.",
